;; repr/asm's read level's classes (doc/asm/SPEC.md §8; doc/asm/AMD64-SURVEY.md §12, AX1 "the rest classed"): every row of
;; test/asm/roundtrip-results-amd64.edn that does not pass is in the first class whose :match finds its REASON, in goi's format.
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :intel
  :title "Intel syntax"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a file read in Intel syntax (its first llvm-mc run's -x86-asm-syntax=intel, or a part after .intel_syntax) that the reader refuses and that is no error test: none since AX3, which reads Intel's operand grammar and MASM's symbol rule (doc/asm/AMD64-SURVEY.md §4.1, P3; AX1's 152 files and AX1's passes of Intel text read as AT&T now read as Intel); kept for an Intel construct the reader does not take yet"
  :decided "AX1's scope (doc/asm/AMD64-SURVEY.md §12); emptied by AX3"
  :match [#"^(error-test )?refused intel: " #"^intel-run refused "]}
 {:id :error-test
  :title "an error test rejected"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the test's RUN lines say llvm-mc rejects it (`not llvm-mc`) and repr/asm's reader rejects it too, at the syntax level; that the rejection is the test's, with the message fragment its CHECK lines state, is AX2's judge (doc/asm/AMD64-SURVEY.md §4.3, §8.1)"
  :decided "AX1's scope (doc/asm/AMD64-SURVEY.md §12)"
  :match [#"^error-test refused "]}
 {:id :error-input
  :title "an input of an error test"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a file of Inputs/ that another test of the directory reads under `not llvm-mc` (non-english-characters.s: a section name with bytes outside ASCII, which LLVM's lexer refuses as an invalid character); repr/asm refuses it as well; AX2 judges the message"
  :decided "AX1's scope"
  :ids ["mc-asmparser/Inputs-non-english-characters-section-name"]
  :match []}
 {:id :lexer-option
  :title "a lexer option of llvm-mc"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the test runs llvm-mc with an option that changes the lexer, which repr/asm does not take: none since 2026-11-17, when the reader takes -motorola-integers ($hex, %binary) and -masm-integers (MASM's radix suffixes, 0B0h, 10h, 0x10h) as the dialect's :motorola-integers and :masm-integers (AXS35 (a), its three files read); kept for another lexer option"
  :decided "AX1's scope; emptied by AXS35 (a), 2026-11-17"
  :ids []
  :match []}
 {:id :other-arch
  :title "a test of another target"
  :kind :design
  :why "the test's RUN lines name no x86 triple (MC/AsmParser's few target-generic tests run on aarch64): arm64's crop reads it (doc/asm/ARM64-SURVEY.md)"
  :decided "AXS1 (a), two crops (the user, 2026-11-09)"
  :match [#"^other-arch "]}
 {:id :not-input
  :title "a test file that is not assembly"
  :kind :design
  :why "the test's RUN lines never give the file itself (%s) to llvm-mc: it holds the RUN and CHECK lines of a test whose inputs are in Inputs/ (pad-for-align-debug.s: its `;` comment lines are statements to an assembler)"
  :decided "AX1's scope"
  :match [#"^not-input "]}
]
